From 8f8aa4a56bf1c3db50c2bca21d9d3f065e7cf7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:26:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dma/gs: PATH2 GIF reassembly, safer IPU/VIF1 DMA, review 55
 G12/G13/G15

- G13: a PACKED/REGLIST GIF packet split across processVIF1Data calls (the
  title writes VIF1_FIFO directly) is held until complete and submitted whole;
  what is still held when the DIRECT ends is passed on incomplete, so a bad
  packet cannot swallow the next one. The state lives beside the interpreter,
  not in PS2Memory (its layout is compiled into generated code). VIF1_FIFO
  writes are counted and logged.
- G12: fromIPU DMA validates the whole RAM destination before taking output or
  touching MADR/QWC instead of masking a KSEG/IO address into RAM; a refused
  toIPU tag leaves the channel registers alone; the VIF1 download honours
  MADR.SPR and resolves its destination before taking a qword from the GS.
- G15: GA2_DMA_TRACE reads are bounded; a CHCR read that clears a still-set STR
  is reported per channel; GA2_IPU_TRACE is read once; GS::reset takes the
  backend lifetime lock; IMAGE tags no longer apply PRE/PRIM; the PATH3 IMAGE
  test walks every tag of a submission; the arbiter gives back oversized
  packet buffers; the pipeline cache is copied under the lock and written from
  a short-lived thread; larger-than-NLOOP uploads become consecutive IMAGE tags;
  gamepad sticks get a radial dead zone; the SPU queue push is two memcpys.
- A5: XGKICK's GIF call-out runs under the default rounding mode, not the
  VU's round-toward-zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
